      "notes": "Partial: AIN0..AIN3 are ideal high-impedance (1 GOhm) ADC probes, so firmware can read the solved node voltage of each (run_firmware with attach_devices feeds the codes; 8-bit over 'vref'). AOUT is an ideal Thevenin source at 'aout' with 'rout' (the real part has a buffered output). Set 'aout' directly, or via apply_firmware_device from the bytes firmware writes (control byte then data, DAC enabled). The read pipeline (the PCF8591 returns the previous conversion first), auto-increment timing, conversion delay, EXT/OSC and the digital bus itself are not modelled. Pin order follows DIP-16 (pin 1 = AIN0, pin 8 = VSS, pin 16 = VDD)."
